{
  "about": "What every HL7 v2 message modeled on a sample shares. A message type's profile (hl7v2-adt.json; -ack, -dft, -mdm, -orm, -oru, -siu, -vxu) extends this one and says what repeats. HL7's syntax -- delimiters, repetitions, MSH counting its field separator, the batch envelope -- is the reader's. Places are written 'PID PID05-1' (PID-5.1), fields numbered as HL7 numbers them.",
  "syntax": "hl7v2",

  "member": {
    "about": "Segments that are the member's: the patient and the insured. A masking algorithm's name is read as a member element only here (a doctor's name in PV1 is not the member's); places listed below hold wherever they are.",
    "segments": ["PID", "IN1"]
  },

